    "optionsVersion": 1,
    "apiVersion": "VERSION_0",
    "isResourceIntensiveScript": false,
    "showPartitioning": false,
    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Compares forecasts with actuals per item and model: MAE, RMSE, MAPE, sMAPE, WAPE, bias and tracking signal, with flags, best model per item and a model ranking.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Supply Chain",
    "tags": [
        "forecast accuracy",
        "wape",
        "mape",
        "bias",
        "tracking signal",
        "demand planning",
        "supply chain",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Measures how good forecasts are, for one model or several side by side (statistical forecast, sales team, naive), per item and overall:\n\n| Measure | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| MAE, RMSE | average absolute error, and root mean squared error (punishes big misses) |\n| MAPE, sMAPE | average percentage error (rows with actual 0 excluded), and its symmetric version |\n| **WAPE**, Accuracy | total absolute error / total actual (the measure most supply chains report), and 1 - WAPE |\n| **Bias** | total (forecast - actual) / total actual: positive = over-forecasting |\n| **Tracking signal** | cumulative error / MAE in period order; beyond about +/-4 the forecast is consistently off |\n\nItems with bias beyond a limit or an out-of-control tracking signal are **flagged**, each item's **best model** is marked, and the models are ranked overall. A row-level output gives every error for charts and drill-down.\n\nInput: one row per item and period with the actual and one or more forecast fields.",
    "dependencies": "",
